From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: What dwm confirms does not undo what Win32 has decided since.

dwm.exe decides nothing about a window's state: it only confirms what
Win32 asked for, later. A program restored from the taskbar that sets its
placement meanwhile (Chromium does) got the confirmation of an older state,
and WS_MAXIMIZE went while the window kept its size: minimized a second
time, it came back not maximized.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
index 9a36798..01c8058 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -611,7 +611,10 @@ static void wayland_configure_window(HWND hwnd)
     if (rect.left == rect.right || rect.bottom == rect.top) flags |= SWP_NOSIZE;
 
     style = NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE);
-    if (!(state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED) != !(style & WS_MAXIMIZE)
+    /* dwm.exe only confirms the state Win32 asked for: a confirmation that
+     * comes after Win32 has changed its mind again must not undo it */
+    if (!process_wayland.arctic_shell_v1
+        && !(state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED) != !(style & WS_MAXIMIZE)
         && !(state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN))
     {
         arctic_log_configure(hwnd, (style & WS_MAXIMIZE) ? "un-maximized" : "maximized", width, height,
